PATIENT INFORMATION

Disclaimer: The severity of the burns requires prolonged intensive care, multiple surgical debridements, and extensive grafting.
Clinical Course: The patient will likely require emergency intubation in the ambulance or immediately upon arrival at the ED to secure the airway before the swelling causes total obstruction.

SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

The spouse must not attempt to transport the patient privately. Do not apply any creams, ice, or home remedies to the burn wounds, as this induces severe hypothermia and tissue damage.

PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: The explosion caused deep burns over a third of his body and burned his airway. Because the skin barrier is gone, he is losing massive amounts of fluid and body heat, causing his blood pressure to drop dangerously low. The IV fluids are replacing the lost volume to keep his heart pumping, and the pure oxygen is treating the smoke inhalation until the paramedics take over his airway.
Actionable Steps: Follow the paramedics immediately to the hospital. Do not touch the burned areas. Provide the hospital with his exact weight (80kg) for fluid calculations.

